Q: Growing a shiny reactive value with a loop and plotting it continuously A: <p>Sorry for posting this in the wrong place. I can't seem to find 'How do I...' questions, though. Should I repost the question in a different segment of Stack Overflow?</p>
<p>For the time being, regarding invalidateLater: thanks for the pointer. Unfortunately I cannot wrap my head around it and apply it to my problem. I am trying to grow the reactive value res() for each value of i in the loop</p>
<pre><code>for(i in 1:input$iterations){...}
</code></pre>
<p>upon pressing the actionbutton. Everytime res() has grown (i. e. after the loop went through one iteration), the plots in output$scatter, output$histogram, ... (the real app has more than two outputs which depend on res()) shall be updated, until the loop has gone through all iterations.</p>
<p>When I run the following, I get the error &quot;Error in plot.window: need finite 'xlim' values&quot; for the scatter plot and &quot;Error in hist.default: 'x' must be numeric&quot; (I assume, because res() has not been processed properly and is still empty):</p>
<pre class="lang-r prettyprint-override"><code>example_function = function(integer){
  1/integer
  # I moved Sys.sleep() into the function; it only exists to simulate a function which takes some time to execute 
  Sys.sleep(1)
}

ui &lt;- fluidPage(
  shiny::selectInput(&quot;iterations&quot;, &quot;Select the number of iterations&quot;, 1:10),
  actionButton(&quot;go1&quot;, label = &quot;Plot result&quot;),
  plotOutput(&quot;scatter&quot;, height = 400), 
  plotOutput(&quot;hist&quot;, height = 400)
)
server &lt;- function(input, output, session){
  res &lt;- eventReactive(input$go1, {
    invalidateLater(1000, session)
    tmp &lt;- c()
    for(i in 1:isolate(input$iterations)){
      tmp &lt;- c(tmp, example_function(i))
      return(tmp)
    }
  })

  output$scatter &lt;- renderPlot({
    invalidateLater(2000, session)
    plot(res())
  })
  output$hist &lt;- renderPlot({
    invalidateLater(2000, session)
    hist(res())
  })
} 

shinyApp(ui = ui, server = server)
</code></pre>
<p>Another problem down the road will be, that I do not understand how to set a condition for stopping the re-evalution once the loop is finished. It says on the documentation page that it is possible to do so, but it doesn't say how.</p>
<p>Any advice on how to apply invalidateLater to my problem?</p>
<p>Thanks!</p>

Q: How to handle Mapbox GL JS popup click events with custom HTML A: <p>Mapbox popups are added to the page only when they open, so normal click listeners won’t work directly.</p>
<h4>Best and Clean Way</h4>
<p>Listen for clicks on the document and catch popup buttons when they appear.</p>
<pre><code>document.addEventListener(&quot;click&quot;, (e) =&gt; {
  if (e.target.classList.contains(&quot;popup-btn&quot;)) {
    console.log(&quot;Popup button clicked&quot;);
  }
});

popup.setHTML(`&lt;button class=&quot;popup-btn&quot;&gt;Click&lt;/button&gt;`);
</code></pre>
<h4>Quick and Simple</h4>
<p>Inline click (okay for small demos):</p>
<pre><code>popup.setHTML(`&lt;button onclick=&quot;alert('Clicked')&quot;&gt;Click&lt;/button&gt;`);
</code></pre>
<h4>For Bigger or Complex UI</h4>
<p>Create the popup with real DOM and attach events normally:</p>
<pre><code>const el = document.createElement(&quot;div&quot;);
el.innerHTML = `&lt;button id=&quot;btn&quot;&gt;Click&lt;/button&gt;`;

el.querySelector(&quot;#btn&quot;).addEventListener(&quot;click&quot;, () =&gt; {
  alert(&quot;Clicked&quot;);
});

popup.setDOMContent(el);
</code></pre>
<h4>Final Tip</h4>
<p>For simple popups, use event delegation.</p>
<p>For interactive popups, use <code>setDOMContent()</code>.</p>
